# grem CLI

The grem CLI stamps deterministic project structure and emits agent-facing
prompts. It does not run an LLM or perform prompted lifecycle changes itself.

## Commands

- `grem scaffold TEMPLATE TARGET` creates the declared folders and copies the
  declared template files into an absent or empty target.
- `grem instructions [PROJECT]` reads [[grem-config]] and prints the prompt for
  aligning configured agent instruction files.
- `grem diff A B` validates two project-local scopes and prints the semantic
  comparison prompt for a numbered list of inconsistencies.
- `grem sync A B` validates the same kinds of scopes and prints the full plan →
  implement → test → document → diff loop.
- `grem upgrade [PROJECT]` requires a clean Git worktree, overlays a newer
  template, and prints the target template's prompt for reviewing and merging
  the resulting unstaged diff. `--interactive` confirms before writing.

`scaffold` and `upgrade` write project files. `diff`, `sync`, and `instructions`
only produce text for a user to copy into an LLM agent such as Claude or Codex.

## Layers

The CLI layer loads and validates declarations, config, and SemVer values.
Template content owns generated project knowledge and agent behavior.

See [[grem-config]].
